1
00:00:34,180 --> 00:00:37,430
Excuse me. My name is Richard Stewart.

2
00:00:37,430 --> 00:00:38,860
I'm a photographer.

3
00:00:38,860 --> 00:00:40,550
May I take a picture of you and your little boy?

4
00:00:40,550 --> 00:00:41,410
What's it for?

5
00:00:41,410 --> 00:00:41,940
It's for a book.

6
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:42,480
Richard Stewart, 46 Linden Street,

7
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:44,180
You're writing a book?

8
00:00:44,180 --> 00:00:45,540
It's a book of pictures.

9
00:00:45,540 --> 00:00:47,230
I call it Family Album, U.S.A.

10
00:00:47,230 --> 00:00:49,300
Oh, that's a nice idea.

11
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:51,230
Well, it's fine if you take our picture.

12
00:00:51,230 --> 00:00:52,810
I'm Martha Vann.

13
00:00:52,810 --> 00:00:55,890
Thank you. I appreciate your help.

14
00:00:55,890 --> 00:00:57,810
I'm Richard. What's your name?

15
00:00:57,810 --> 00:00:58,990
Gerald.

16
00:00:58,990 --> 00:00:59,920
How old are you, Gerald?

17
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:01,060
Five.

18
00:01:01,060 --> 00:01:02,050
And where do you live?

19
00:01:02,050 --> 00:01:03,580
We live in California.

20
00:01:03,580 --> 00:01:07,290
Well, welcome to New York.

21
00:01:07,290 --> 00:01:10,770
OK, just a second.

22
00:01:10,770 --> 00:01:12,440
I'm almost ready here.

23
00:01:12,440 --> 00:01:13,800
Can I help you?

24
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:21,760
Oh, please.

25
00:01:21,760 --> 00:01:28,530
Hold Gerald's hand, please. Great!

26
00:01:28,530 --> 00:01:32,840
Now point to the buildings.

27
00:01:32,840 --> 00:01:36,460
Terrific!

28
00:01:36,460 --> 00:01:43,710
Give Mommy a kiss, Gerald. Nice!

29
00:01:43,710 --> 00:01:45,970
Thank you, Gerald.

30
00:01:45,970 --> 00:01:47,640
And thank you, Mrs. Vann.

31
00:01:47,640 --> 00:01:48,450
Oh, my pleasure.

32
00:01:48,450 --> 00:01:50,230
We'll be looking for your book.

33
00:01:50,230 --> 00:01:56,300
Thank you. Good-bye. Bye, Gerald.

34
00:01:56,300 --> 00:01:58,330
Thanks again.

35
00:01:58,330 --> 00:02:00,100
Oh, you're welcome.

36
00:02:00,100 --> 00:02:01,950
Hey, let me take your picture!

37
00:02:01,950 --> 00:02:10,170
Wonderful. Please.

38
00:02:10,170 --> 00:02:11,500
Are you from New York?

39
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:13,220
No, I'm from Greece.

40
00:02:13,220 --> 00:02:15,850
I'm an exchange student.

41
00:02:15,850 --> 00:02:17,330
When did you come here?

42
00:02:17,330 --> 00:02:18,970
Three months ago.

43
00:02:18,970 --> 00:02:20,780
Your English is very good.

44
00:02:20,780 --> 00:02:22,320
Thanks.

45
00:02:22,320 --> 00:02:28,780
I studied English in school.

46
00:02:28,780 --> 00:02:30,080
Would you like some coffee?

47
00:02:30,080 --> 00:02:32,230
No, thank you.

48
00:02:32,230 --> 00:02:34,220
Tell me about your book.

49
00:02:34,220 --> 00:02:36,260
Oh, it's not finished yet,

50
00:02:36,260 --> 00:02:37,820
but I have some of the pictures.

51
00:02:37,820 --> 00:02:38,850
Would you like to see them?

52
00:02:38,850 --> 00:02:40,770
Yes. I'd like that.

53
00:02:40,770 --> 00:02:48,140
Here they are. Family Album, U.S.A.

54
00:02:48,140 --> 00:02:50,280
It's an album of pictures of the United States:

55
00:02:50,280 --> 00:02:53,530
the cities, the special places, and the people.

56
00:02:53,530 --> 00:02:56,380
And these are pictures of people working:

57
00:02:56,380 --> 00:03:06,610
steelworkers, bankers, police, street vendors,

58
00:03:06,610 --> 00:03:11,100
ambulance drivers, doctors....

59
00:03:11,100 --> 00:03:16,390
Oh, this is my father. He's a doctor.

60
00:03:16,390 --> 00:03:17,880
This is my mother.

61
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:18,650
What's her name?

62
00:03:18,650 --> 00:03:21,900
Ellen.

63
00:03:21,900 --> 00:03:23,350
My younger brother, Robbie.

64
00:03:23,350 --> 00:03:25,650
He goes to high school.

65
00:03:25,650 --> 00:03:27,470
This is my sister Susan.

66
00:03:27,470 --> 00:03:31,130
She works for a toy company.

67
00:03:31,130 --> 00:03:35,260
Here's my grandfather. He lives in Florida.

68
00:03:35,260 --> 00:03:37,310
And this is my wife Marilyn.

69
00:03:37,310 --> 00:03:38,700
Oh, she's very pretty.

70
00:03:38,700 --> 00:03:42,420
Thanks. And what about your family?

71
00:03:42,420 --> 00:03:44,920
They are in Thessaloniki.

72
00:03:44,920 --> 00:03:47,440
That's a large city in northern Greece.

73
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:50,340
But now I'm living in the Bronx.

74
00:03:50,340 --> 00:03:52,030
With a Greek-American family?

75
00:03:52,030 --> 00:03:57,980
No. Hispanic.

76
00:03:57,980 --> 00:04:01,810
Oh no! It's five thirty.

77
00:04:01,810 --> 00:04:02,840
Will you excuse me?

78
00:04:02,840 --> 00:04:05,180
I have to meet my wife.

79
00:04:05,180 --> 00:04:06,460
It was nice meeting you.

80
00:04:06,460 --> 00:04:08,260
It was a pleasure meeting you, too.

81
00:04:08,260 --> 00:04:09,740
Thanks for your help.

82
00:04:09,740 --> 00:04:12,460
And good luck! I've got to go.

83
00:04:12,460 --> 00:04:14,030
By the way, I'm Richard.

84
00:04:14,030 --> 00:04:14,780
What's your name?

85
00:04:14,780 --> 00:04:16,290
Alexandra.

86
00:04:16,290 --> 00:04:17,170
Bye-bye, Alexandra. Thanks.

87
00:04:17,170 --> 00:04:20,170
Bye-bye. Richard! Richard! You left your bag!
